{"full":"hf:A19grey/Depth-Pro-in-Meters","spaceId":"A19grey/Depth-Pro-in-Meters","name":"Depth-Pro-in-Meters","source":"huggingface","description":"An interactive AI application on Hugging Face Spaces.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","topics":["gradio","region:us"],"technologies":["Python"],"likes":52,"created":"2024-10-04T20:08:41.000Z","updated":"2025-07-01T22:04:27.000Z","license":null,"runtime":"RUNNING","appUrl":"https://a19grey-depth-pro-in-meters.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/A19grey/Depth-Pro-in-Meters","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T07:29:26.034Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T07:29:26.034Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T07:29:26.034Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"🚀","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This software project accompanies the research paper: Depth Pro: Sharp Monocular Metric Depth in Less Than a Second, Aleksei Bochkovskii, Amaël Delaunoy, Hugo Germain, Marcel Santos, Yichao Zhou, Stephan R. Richter, and Vladlen Koltun.","We present a foundation model for zero-shot metric monocular depth estimation. Our model, Depth Pro, synthesizes high-resolution depth maps with unparalleled sharpness and high-frequency details. The predictions are metric, with absolute scale, without relying on the availability of metadata such as camera intrinsics. And the model is fast, producing a 2.25-megapixel depth map in 0.3 seconds on a standard GPU. These characteristics are enabled by a number of technical contributions, including an efficient multi-scale vision transformer for dense prediction, a training protocol that combines…","The model in this repository is a reference implementation, which has been re-trained. Its performance is close to the model reported in the paper but does not match it exactly."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/A19grey/Depth-Pro-in-Meters/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"fa34fc76d604f3c1b30b19abf61260ade864ad2a